column2:
This contest, the harmless one, has been finished;
6	now another mark, which no man has yet hit,
7	I shall know whether I can reach, and Apollo grant me glory.

Friends, will not someone go up to the side-door
133	and tell the people, and a shout would quickly arise;
134	then this man would soon shoot for the last time.

Come here, rise, old woman born long ago, who are the
396	overseer of the maidservants in our halls;
397	come; my father calls you, to say something to you.

Rejoice in your heart, old woman, and hold, and do not cry out;
412	it is not holy to boast over slain men.
413	These the fate of the gods subdued, and their cruel deeds;
414	for they honoured no one of men upon the earth,
415	neither bad nor good, whoever came to them;
416	therefore by their wantonness they met a shameful fate.
417	But come, tell me the women in the halls,
418	those who dishonour me and those who are blameless.
